<!--
  Dummy/placeholder driver photo (2026-08-27 fidelity pass, driver-photo dashboard feature).

  No real driver photo asset existed anywhere in the repo before this (confirmed: the whole
  res/ tree had zero person/avatar drawables). The Figma design system itself never draws an
  actual photo here either: every "Avatar / Driver" instance in the approved dashboard frame
  (fileKey JhEhok3n9bntRNS5Y1u3Yc, node 26:20) is a generic white person-glyph icon on a dark
  gradient circle, not a photo. This is a deliberate step beyond that: a small illustrated
  headshot (simple flat-color face/hair/shoulders on a warm gradient background) standing in for
  a real uploaded photo, so the dashboard identity chip reads as "a person's photo" rather than
  "an icon". Used only as the fallback shown until ProfileViewModel's real photo-upload flow
  (see ProfileScreen.kt's IdentityHeader) has a genuine photo loaded for this driver.
-->
